  "reference_answer": "Actually, I've come to enjoy it, but that wasn't always the case. When I first moved out on my own, I saw cooking as a chore—I'd just boil pasta or microwave ready meals because I had no confidence in the kitchen. But over the past couple of years, I've started to see it differently. It's become a way for me to unwind after a long day, especially when I put on some music and take my time with the prep. I also love the social side of it—inviting friends over and cooking for them gives me a real sense of pride. That said, I'm not into fancy or complicated dishes; I stick to simple, hearty meals that I know will turn out well. So yes, I genuinely enjoy it now, mainly because it's become more about connection and relaxation than just feeding myself.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "以时间变化为主线：从讨厌做饭到享受做饭，原因是它从任务变成了放松和社交的方式，并强调只做简单可靠的菜。",
