  "reference_answer": "To be honest, I wouldn't say I love cooking, but I do enjoy it under the right circumstances. My enjoyment really depends on who I'm cooking for. When I'm just making something for myself, I tend to see it as a bit of a chore—I'll grab whatever's quick, like eggs on toast or instant noodles. But when I'm cooking for other people, it's a completely different story. I get a real kick out of planning a menu, picking out fresh ingredients, and then seeing everyone enjoy what I've made. There's something deeply satisfying about that. For instance, last month I hosted a small dinner for a few friends and made a slow-cooked beef stew. Watching them go back for seconds made all the effort worthwhile. So I suppose my answer is: I enjoy cooking, but mainly as a social activity rather than a daily routine.",
  "reference_angle_summary": "主线：是否享受烹饪取决于为谁做饭——为自己做饭视为杂务，为他人做饭则乐在其中。示例为朋友做炖牛肉。",
